ee whose limb (c) fails.\n\nI have checked POL-NS-05: the arrival marker is not false. At the arrival timestamp the trace places the driver at the pin (min_distance_m 0.0) and stationary (0.0 kph), and the qualifying run starts at that moment (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), so no false-arrival record can be referred under POL-NS-05(ii) and the waiting clock is not recomputed.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02708-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). It cures nothing: POL-NS-06(i) allows separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only on a present and populated advisory, so the 229-second single run stands as the whole dwell and the shortfall cannot be closed. The rider's claim invoking that artifact was discarded at the citation stage for not naming its issue code, and I have not relied on it; but the artifact is cited nowhere in the reasoning that decides this case.\n\nThe evidence is unimpaired for policy purposes. The GPS trace shows 100% coverage, 80 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0; the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count; and the fare line matches the policy figure. No POL-NS-08 limb (a) to (d) fires, and no POL-NS-09(e) escalation arises. No other escalation trigger fires either: neither profile shows repeat disputes between these parties (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0), the rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 0 against completed_trips_30d 132), so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged.\n\nNo referral is recorded. POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged because the marker was true, and the POL-NS-01 driver-education referral for a mis-selected reason code is not engaged either: RIDER_NO_SHOW is one of the codes limb (d) recognises, and the defect here is the short waiting time, not the code chosen. For completeness, the driver's stated reason for leaving early is a matter a human reviewer may wish to look at, bu